 Godly Niche  hopefully we'll find out sooner rather  than later  if the mid-credit Stingers set up new  conflicts the end credit scene puts some  to rest Heimdall the Asgardian Warrior  and protector of the bifrost was slain  by Thanos early on in Avengers Infinity  War since he fought bravely as a viking  and perished in battle we could safely  assume he ascended to the paradise of  Valhalla audiences recently got a peek  at another version of the afterlife in  Moon Knight when Oscar Isaac's Mark  Spector and Steven Grant died for a  while their brief visit came with the  explanation that there are many versions  of what we might call Heavens in the  universe and Multiverse the field of  reads is one as Guardians Valhalla is  another Thor love and thunder shows us  the mcu's Valhalla for the first time  when Jane who had passed away in Thor's  Embrace only moments before arrives at  its entrance waiting for her is Heimdall  to tell her that the Asgardian version  of the afterlife is now her Eternal  reward the film ends as Jane Smiles at  the breathtakingly beautiful landscape  that stands before her this scene could  well be a last goodbye to the tooth orca  characters but since there are stories  that take place in Valhalla and Marvel  Comics we shouldn't consider Jane or  Heimdall to be permanently gone from the  MCU just yet check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more Looper  videos about the Marvel Cinematic  Universe are coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and hit the Bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

